            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0146" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/8–948: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-08-12T15:00:00-04:00">August 12, 1948—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1166. White House states (urtel 1466, Aug. 9) “that the President never made any
                    statement about military aid to China to Mr. Wellington <pb facs="0147" n="137"
                        xml:id="pg137"/> Koo. The only comment the President made was one to the
                    effect that he hoped that we would all some day see a strong, united China”.
                    Dept relies on your discretion to effect such correction as you think desirable
                    informally and without publicity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
